=== (b) Jacobian rank of 2-local couplings -> spectrum, modulo local unitaries ===
   n  P(2-local)  P-3n  2^n-1  rank J  fibre dim = P-3n-rank   verdict        min level gap
   3         36     27      7       7                    20   NON-UNIQUE      1.49e+00
   4         66     54     15      15                    39   NON-UNIQUE      5.22e-01
   5        105     90     31      31                    59   NON-UNIQUE      2.01e-01
   6        153    135     63      63                    72   NON-UNIQUE      9.75e-02
   7        210    189    127     127                    62   NON-UNIQUE      3.68e-02
   8        276    252    255     252                     0   LOCALLY UNIQUE  1.76e-02
   9        351    324    511     324                     0   LOCALLY UNIQUE  1.52e-02
  10        435    405   1023     405                     0   LOCALLY UNIQUE  3.67e-03
  image dimension of the 2-local family in spectrum space = rank; spectrum space dim = 2^n - 1
  -> once P-3n < 2^n-1 (here n >= 8) the image is a proper submanifold: a Lebesgue-null set of spectra admits ANY 2-local TPS

